BRL-CAD on macOS README
=======================

macOS is supported on a best-effort basis.  While BRL-CAD is regularly
built and tested on macOS in Continuous Integration, prebuilt macOS
binary installers (.dmg) are not provided for every release.  Check the
GitHub Releases page (https://github.com/BRL-CAD/brlcad/releases) for
availability; if no macOS installer is posted for a given release, you
will need to build from source (or run a Linux environment/container).

Table of Contents
-----------------
  Support Status
  Prerequisites
  Building from Source
  Debugging
  Tips
  Bugs

Support Status
--------------
- Prebuilt Binaries: Provided intermittently (for example, Apple Silicon
  arm64 .dmg installers on select releases).  Not every release ships a
  macOS package.
- Architecture: Modern builds target Apple Silicon (arm64) and Intel
  (x86_64) macOS with Apple Clang.  Universal (fat) binaries are not
  supported.
- GUI Support: Classic Tcl/Tk interfaces (MGED, Archer) require XQuartz
  (X11).  Experimental Qt support (qged) can be enabled with
  -DBRLCAD_ENABLE_QT=ON.

Prerequisites
-------------
To build BRL-CAD from source on macOS, install:

1. Xcode Command Line Tools (Apple Clang, C++17 support):
     xcode-select --install

2. CMake (3.26 or later):
     https://cmake.org/download/   (or: brew install cmake)

3. XQuartz (required for X11 / Tk GUIs such as mged and archer):
     brew install --cask xquartz

4. OpenSSL 3:
     brew install openssl@3

Building from Source
--------------------
Clone the repository and configure with CMake:

  git clone https://github.com/BRL-CAD/brlcad.git
  cd brlcad
  OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR="$(brew --prefix openssl@3)"
  export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR/lib/pkgconfig${PKG_CONFIG_PATH:+:$PKG_CONFIG_PATH}"
  cmake -S . -B build \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
    -DBRLCAD_BUNDLED_LIBS=ON \
    -DOPENSSL_ROOT_DIR="$OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR" \
    -DCMAKE_REQUIRE_FIND_PACKAGE_OpenSSL=ON
  cmake --build build -j4
  cmake --build build --target check

To enable Qt-based tools (such as qged), add -DBRLCAD_ENABLE_QT=ON to
the CMake configure command.

Debugging
---------
Apple employs code signing and BRL-CAD development binaries are not
signed by default.  To debug locally built apps using lldb or
Instruments, sign them with get-task-allow entitlements:

  echo '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "https://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd"><plist version="1.0"><dict><key>com.apple.security.get-task-allow</key><true/></dict></plist>' > debug.plist
  codesign -s - -v -f --entitlements debug.plist build/bin/*

Tips
----
To check your macOS version and CPU architecture when reporting issues:

  sw_vers -productVersion
  uname -a

Bugs
----
macOS-specific issues (such as X11/XQuartz or Tk display limitations)
can be reported at https://github.com/BRL-CAD/brlcad/issues.  Refer to
the top-level BUGS file for general known issues.
